// obj/rsoul.lpc: genuinely lost content. The original archive's entire
// implementation was a single #include of a wizard's own personal file,
// "/players/moonchild/misc/rsoul.mudlib.lpc" -- which is completely
// absent from this archive (checked both the raw, unconverted tarball
// and the converted work tree; no trace anywhere, under any name).
// Every new character crashes here (doc/lib/player.lpc's own
// move_player_to_start3() does `clone_object("obj/rsoul")->
// move_object(myself);` unconditionally, uncaught) with "No program in
// object '/obj/rsoul'!", aborting mid-function and silently skipping
// everything after it -- including the actual move into the starting
// room, which is why a brand new character never physically arrives
// anywhere at all. Since the real "remote soul" command set can't be
// recovered, this is a minimal inert stand-in: it exists, compiles, and
// does nothing, so cloning/moving it no longer crashes and character
// setup can actually finish. See AGENTS.md, NOTES.md.

int id(string str) {
  return str == "rsoul" || str == "racesoul";
}

string short() {
  return 0;
}

int invis() {
  return 1;
}
